[{"id":"VRCE-5-21-1","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":21,"verse":1,"english":"Having spoken thus Maithili and commanded the host of the Räksasīs, Rāvana, a terror to his enemies, went away.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.875,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5021001","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0aa79068ce503d837a913fccc4a9812fcdb49d5c0cfef76a29bd134c6f52120e","compact":"2bad6f60e4a5ff3da137130eb36305ba9734e14e65037c487b42f3916b236a33","nasal":"2bad6f60e4a5ff3da137130eb36305ba9734e14e65037c487b42f3916b236a33"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-21-2","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":21,"verse":2,"english":"And after that lord of Rākşasas had gone away and entered his inner apartment, the hideous Rākşasīs drew near Sitä.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5021002","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0cf9f1a52233c98c653b7f5fde1b93e3ff9bdb8702ca1ac6922a7e262ff9627a","compact":"d6c9ce94bcec602a5e0bd3721ec019297f83022eeffc3129328ba2cc41ebde47","nasal":"53cb1a83fd4c73c9a8e0b538d81f631da4fe027469a3fef9827a871c6aaf78b2"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-21-3","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":21,"verse":3,"english":"And approaching Sītā that terrible host, almost faint with ire, addressed Vaidehī with the following harsh words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5021003","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d40d346b46ce0291deca5a7b9d71309f22e56f2b3ed5d3e1ecf5fc6665642d32","compact":"45cc34128cc4a63b2cf3ce7581b6c87877aec645de73371d3c4f4c421188eb28","nasal":"45cc34128cc4a63b2cf3ce7581b6c87877aec645de73371d3c4f4c421188eb28"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-21-4","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":21,"verse":4,"english":"You do not regard it highly, Sītā, that you shall become the chosen wife of that highsouled, and great Ravana, the Ten-necked son of Paulastya.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5021004","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1d7d875313202f70eeb86128170e53f76eeb11e92022dbd1e02dbd301c7cf191","compact":"e312f44908f56b2f0888e443ba414cacf6b59a088babff043d6df53a830e217b","nasal":"e312f44908f56b2f0888e443ba414cacf6b59a088babff043d6df53a830e217b"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-21-5","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":21,"verse":5,"english":"Thereupon another Rākṣasī named Ekjatä, with eyes rendered coppery with ire, addressing Sītā, having a small navel, said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.955,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5021005","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f534f816af5be342e770e51b3da6ac02518284ac51c38db81c9d26b807d6b241","compact":"166926872778ff6836729d45f01c1a7cc4a8a6d048d8e71dd133a37020f3a56e","nasal":"af1634fca2829064be425f53f4e93814190816a47154a73c5d10ae589cd4dd58"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-21-6","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":21,"verse":6,"english":"Pulastya is the fourth of the six Prajāpatīs, (Prajāpatis are the lords of the created being first created by Brahmā.) a mind-born son of Brahmā and celebrated in the world.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.882,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5021006","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6039081ea1dc5b4eb7292493ca252f14154cefb7759a1ce32bcbca25f5be236a","compact":"d6ea8c1a885f1e66cbab5eafe027eb90b3547733a351481ea1fbe642b5203439","nasal":"96246bf67d442a379d8c6438d150344e7db4da00f04c23cc929a5ce344d79107"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-21-7","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":21,"verse":7,"english":"The glorious ascetic, by name Vishravā was the mind-born son to Pulastya, effulgent like to Prajāpatis.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5021007","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b5d16d518b682c255cc377b9ff77d134ceef47675d53827be53feb4df89b76c5","compact":"c3921f913aa0f411b9ddab2260d0cdc22782dcc54763af28bb9bf7adf4e8e1f0","nasal":"c3921f913aa0f411b9ddab2260d0cdc22782dcc54763af28bb9bf7adf4e8e1f0"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-21-8","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":21,"verse":8,"english":"O large-eyed damsel! Of Visravā came Rāvana terrible to his enemies. And it behove you to become the consort of that lord of Raksasas. Scorn not the words I say to you, O you of comely presence.” Thereupon another Rākşasī named Harijatā, having the eyes of a cat, and whirling them with ire, said It become you to be the wife of that lord of Rākşasas who smote the thirty three celestials and their lord in battle.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-8","DUTT-5-23-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5021008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b21eefed5a5ced64af6ab08157b43fcdc6bf0f9a084e4e28ceefd0e4cebf353a","compact":"9c64129e0d0326566f5c2ed4e6f5f2b4f6746d3cd779de6b70ed6f648e183700","nasal":"5859cfae0b84febe96fd8e8eede044a4f79f3c09b6d3844793295c7b5c198ee7"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-21-9","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":21,"verse":9,"english":"Thereupon another Rākşasī named Harijatā, having the eyes of a cat, and whirling them with ire, said It become you to be the wife of that lord of Rākşasas who smote the thirty three celestials and their lord in battle.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5021009","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1b8b7d7dbbb3b36f539dd502b2ad035535041e03ff6411018118025ab655b257","compact":"86a2c3026740309d4b5d3e7b4762fc460c044c3f2f018f77c91d95b090e071b3","nasal":"86a2c3026740309d4b5d3e7b4762fc460c044c3f2f018f77c91d95b090e071b3"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-21-10","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":21,"verse":10,"english":"O large-eyed damsel! Of Visravā came Rāvana terrible to his enemies. And it behove you to become the consort of that lord of Raksasas. Scorn not the words I say to you, O you of comely presence.” Thereupon another Rākşasī named Harijatā, having the eyes of a cat, and whirling them with ire, said It become you to be the wife of that lord of Rākşasas who smote the thirty three celestials and their lord in battle.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-8","DUTT-5-23-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5021010","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8d6087ec7554db416a76bc6b0c586e5bc1a10260dc7da7da6e629cbb263e68c3","compact":"a5ffb14d4a9f8ab3e410ea5223ab9c54085d0fc03be027b6ca0ddd305a6ef708","nasal":"e4705ca16b416b4fe1b30904e20af59ed220b83dd420dd64d5b7a826f596631f"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-21-11","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":21,"verse":11,"english":"Do you not desire to be his wife, who is heroic, of indomitable prowess and who dose not turn back in battle?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.803,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5021011","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8a2e6955bbcc38c36d387f3babc599b3641d4daa3ea980f68d5bd871b2951bd5","compact":"0742bc1efa87c843cc5c75ac04385d3cbff149054f92d7f86e269d58236188ad","nasal":"0742bc1efa87c843cc5c75ac04385d3cbff149054f92d7f86e269d58236188ad"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-21-12","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":21,"verse":12,"english":"And turning away in scorn from his beloved wife, highly esteemed, the mighty king Ravana, desire for you. And leaving his inner apartment enriched with thousand of females and adorned with various jewels, Rāvana shall adore you.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5021012","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cc223f61d2efa9855342ae144453a685887904e32feb081f4a80d19b5a9ecf3f","compact":"2aed00cc101bc2953af680c214b4d7dadcef1768ddbe2684797c320326c0f419","nasal":"2aed00cc101bc2953af680c214b4d7dadcef1768ddbe2684797c320326c0f419"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-21-13","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":21,"verse":13,"english":"And turning away in scorn from his beloved wife, highly esteemed, the mighty king Ravana, desire for you. And leaving his inner apartment enriched with thousand of females and adorned with various jewels, Rāvana shall adore you.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-23-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5021013","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7ac7f5e31f07b560503446a52df882702f2d370b7f281471ab4cd2abbb0d6f7e","compact":"5d61ed00dfc90c77af8495cfb120499a6fb19a75623613d3cc0bb36d4b670bd8","nasal":"0be859c1bc02cc31771f1df3c87c2294069f48345f8d9caca3e2f37a1ee8d849"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-21-14","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga"